---
/**
 * HOLD: DRAFT, NOT FOR main. #143, the page a coach sends a lifter (Logbook, 2026-10-14, branch
 * feat/site-coach-page). Words go to the product lead and Mike before this merges; design and
 * privacy reviews next. noindex and out of TopNav until approved.
 *
 * The "You choose" and "Sharing less later" paragraphs are #140's privacy text (missionbuilt-site
 * feat/coach-for-everyone 4028f41), true from IronStack build 75 with Social 0.6.0; this page
 * can't go up before both are out, and must change with them if they change. IronStack's b75
 * privacy page (feat/ironstack-privacy-b75) must be live first or at the same time.
 *
 * After the design and privacy reviews (2026-10-14): "Where it goes", "The read", "Ending it"
 * and "Coach notes" are the b75 privacy page's approved Coach mode paragraphs (a6c3c48), word
 * for word, so a lifter reads here everything the app says before Accept.
 *
 * #164 (IronStack b76, Tuesday 10-20): "A workout your coach logs for you" and the last sentence of
 * "Ending it" are the #164 privacy page's Coach mode text (feat/ironstack-privacy-coach-logged,
 * f36d97b + 1fcf30a and the 6-hour sweep wording, both rebased 10-17), word for word. That privacy
 * page must be live first or the same day. "The read" leaves out the privacy page's clause pointing to
 * its Anthropic table, on purpose: the table isn't on this page (privacy review 10-17).
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import TopNav from '../../components/TopNav.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Your coach invited you · Mission Built"
  description="Your coach uses IronStack's Coach mode. What to install, how to say yes, and what your coach sees."
  active="coach"
  noindex={true}
>
  <TopNav active="coach" />

  <main id="main" class="page">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/rack">The apps</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true"> / </span>
      <a href="/coach">Coach mode</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true"> / </span>
      <span class="here">Invited</span>
    </nav>

    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        <span class="dots" aria-hidden="true">▮▮▮</span>
        <span>For lifters</span>
        <span class="dots" aria-hidden="true">▮▮▮</span>
      </p>
      <h1 class="display"><span>Your coach invited you</span><span class="dot">.</span></h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Three steps, and you choose what they see.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="block" id="steps">
      <p class="section-label">Get set up</p>
      <h2 class="section-h2">Install, sign in, say yes.</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3 class="v">Install IronStack</h3>
            <p class="body">IronStack is in a TestFlight beta. Sign up with your Apple ID email and mention in the note that your coach invited you; you don't need to name them. The invite comes from Apple.</p>
            <a class="cta" href="/rack/ironstack#beta">Join the IronStack beta →</a>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3 class="v">Sign in to Social</h3>
            <p class="body">Coach mode uses your Social sign‑in. Pick a handle and give it to your coach. Your coach asks by your handle.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <div>
            <h3 class="v">Say yes</h3>
            <p class="body">Nothing is shared until you say yes. You choose what your coach sees before anything is sent. Accepting shares every set (always, since that is the point) and your notes and how you felt; your sleep and bodyweight and your MealStack fueling summary are off unless you turn them on under Customize. You choose how far back: from today (the default), 30, 60 or 90 days, or all your history (earlier versions offer 12 weeks). You can change all of this later in Settings › Coach mode.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="block" id="after">
      <p class="section-label">After that</p>
      <h2 class="section-h2">Your plan, your call.</h2>
      <p class="prose">Their plan arrives as a suggestion; accept it and change anything you like. You lift, and they see every set against the plan: weight, reps, RPE, what you swapped or skipped.</p>
      <div class="fine">
        <p><strong>Where it goes.</strong> When a workout ends, it is sent to Mission Built's Social server at social.missionbuilt.io, on Cloudflare, stored in its database, and passed to your coach's phone. If you share your notes, the server checks them for words like “pain” or “tweak” so it can tell your coach a workout needs a look. We don't use your shared workouts for anything else, and we don't sell them. Edits and deletes follow. Plans your coach sends you, and the short note with them, come the same way, and stay suggestions until you accept them. Coach mode may send you or your coach a notification, through Apple, never between 9 PM and 7 AM unless you change the quiet hours.</p>
        <p><strong>A workout your coach logs for you.</strong> Your coach can log a workout for you on their phone, for example when you train together. When they finish, it goes to Mission Built's Social server and waits there until your phone fetches it, at most 14 days, and the server deletes it within 6 hours after that. Until it reaches our server it waits on your coach's phone; once the server has it, their phone keeps no copy. It lands in your history marked "Logged by @coach" and then follows your sharing choices like any workout. You can delete it: it comes off your history, and if you shared it, its card comes down; your log and its export keep it, like every correction, until you delete your data. It is never written to Apple Health or sent to MealStack. It never carries sleep, bodyweight, fueling, heart rate or location. The server keeps a short record (who, which day, delivered or not) for 30 days, deleted within 6 hours after that, so your coach can see whether it arrived. You can turn this off in Coach mode.</p>
        <p><strong>The read.</strong> Your coach can ask Stack AI to sum up a week of your training, this week or an earlier one. That sends Anthropic your handle, the week's shared workouts (seven days, at most 21 workouts) and a few figures your coach's phone works out from everything you've shared: how each lift's estimated max has moved, which lifts have stalled, and, if you share sleep, how hard your sets felt after nights under 7 hours. Your plan isn't sent, only where the week differed from it. The request comes from your coach's phone and runs on your coach's Stack AI allowance. Mission Built's server passes it on and keeps none of it. You can't turn The read off; ending the link stops it.</p>
        <p><strong>Sharing less later.</strong> If you share less later, the server deletes the workouts and details you stopped sharing from your coach's copy, and your coach's phone deletes them when it next checks in. Server backups drop them within 30 days. We can't take back what your coach already saw, or a week already summed up with Stack AI.</p>
        <p><strong>Ending it.</strong> Either of you can end the link at any time. Ending it, blocking each other, or deleting either Social account deletes your coach's copy on the server (the workouts and the plans), and your coach's phone deletes its copy as soon as it sees the link is gone. Until then, the server keeps each workout until the link ends or you delete that workout in the app. Server backups drop it within 30 days. Ending the link, blocking or deleting either account also deletes any workout your coach logged for you that hasn't reached your phone, and its record.</p>
        <p><strong>Coach notes.</strong> A coach can keep a private note about each lifter. It stays on the coach's phone (and in that phone's own backup), is never sent to us, the lifter or Stack AI, and is deleted when the link ends, on sign-out, or with Delete all.</p>
        <p>Every detail is on <a href="/rack/ironstack/privacy#coach-mode">IronStack's privacy page</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="tail"></div>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter links={[{ label: 'IronStack', href: '/rack/ironstack' }, { label: 'Coach mode', href: '/coach' }, { label: 'IronStack privacy', href: '/rack/ironstack/privacy' }, { label: 'Support', href: '/rack/support' }]} />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page { max-width: 1280px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .breadcrumb {
    padding: 18px var(--pad-page-x) 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-chalk-faint);
  }
  .breadcrumb a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; color: var(--color-chalk-dim); transition: color 120ms ease-out; }
  .breadcrumb a:hover { color: var(--color-chalk); }
  .hero { padding: 40px var(--pad-page-x) 28px; text-align: center; }
  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; margin: 0 0 18px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.24em;
    color: var(--color-chalk-dim); text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .eyebrow .dots { letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--color-blood-bright); }
  .display {
    margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(48px, 10vw, 96px); line-height: 0.95; letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-chalk); text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .display .dot { color: var(--color-blood-bright); }
  .subtitle { margin: 22px auto 0; max-width: 820px; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(16px, 2.4vw, 24px); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-chalk); }
  .block { padding: 56px var(--pad-page-x) 0; max-width: 1180px; }
  .section-label { margin: 0 0 14px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.24em; color: var(--color-blood-text); text-transform: uppercase; }
  .section-h2 { margin: 0 0 18px; max-width: 30ch; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 36px; line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: var(--color-chalk); text-transform: uppercase; }
  .prose { margin: 0 0 16px; max-width: 70ch; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 300; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--color-chalk-dim); }
  .prose a, .fine a { color: var(--color-chalk); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-chalk-ghost); text-decoration: none; }
  .prose a:hover, .fine a:hover { border-bottom-color: var(--color-blood); }
  .k { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-chalk-faint); margin: 0; }
  .fine { margin-top: 18px; background: var(--color-panel); border: var(--border-thin); padding: 22px 26px; }
  .fine .k { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .fine p:not(.k) { margin: 0 0 10px; max-width: 70ch; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-chalk-dim); }
  .fine p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .fine strong { color: var(--color-chalk); font-weight: 700; }
  .steps { margin: 24px 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; counter-reset: step; border-top: var(--border-thin); }
  .steps li { counter-increment: step; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 56px 1fr; gap: 16px; padding: 18px 0; border-bottom: var(--border-thin); }
  .steps li::before { content: counter(step, decimal-leading-zero); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--color-blood-text); }
  .steps .v { margin: 0 0 6px; font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 500; font-size: 20px; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-chalk); }
  .steps .body { margin: 0; max-width: 70ch; font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-chalk-dim); }
  /* The site's one button (QA 10-16). */
  .cta { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; margin-top: 8px; padding: 13px 22px; background: var(--color-blood); border: 1px solid var(--color-blood); font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-chalk); white-space: nowrap; }
  .cta:hover { background: var(--color-blood); }
  .tail { height: 72px; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .breadcrumb { padding: 18px var(--pad-page-x-mobile) 0; }
    .hero { padding: 28px var(--pad-page-x-mobile) 20px; }
    .block { padding: 40px var(--pad-page-x-mobile) 0; }
    .section-h2 { font-size: 28px; }
    .steps li { grid-template-columns: 40px 1fr; }
  }

  /* QA pass 2026-10-16: the box fits its text instead of leaving a strip of empty panel. */
  .fine { max-width: calc(70ch + 52px); }
  .fine p { font-size: 15px; }
  /* Breadcrumb underline on the words, not the 44 pt box; no stacked rules after the last comparison row (iPhone recheck 10-16). */
  .breadcrumb a { border-bottom: 0; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--color-chalk-ghost); text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .vr:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
</style>
